  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "James Danly said that data centers, AI, and reindustrialization have added load to the system at an unprecedented rate and show no signs of slowing. He also said the imperative for the United States to win the AI race is clear. At his nomination hearing, Danly called sufficient generation deployment critical, described AI as an important source of rising demand, and cited a Biden Administration estimate that the United States was about 18 months ahead of China in AI development for language training models.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s3"
   ],
   "sentences": [
